 text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to rip "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move away with violence and speed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When a wild storm ripped the grass from Skara Brae, it exposed an immense refuse heap."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about history and civilizations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Neolithic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "refers to the last part of the Stone Age characterized by domestication of animals, development of agriculture and polished stone instruments"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Neolithic village of Skara Brae was discovered in the winter of 1850. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to expose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make visible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When a wild storm ripped the grass from Skara Brae, it exposed an immense refuse heap"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "refuse heap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " an accumulation of discarded waste materials"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When a wild storm ripped the grass from Skara Brae, it exposed an immense refuse heap."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to bring to light"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to expose, to make visible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It also brought to light the ruins of ancient stone buildings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "semi-subterranean"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "partially underground"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The structures of this semi-subterranean village have survived in impressive condition."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slab"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thick piece"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The houses have been built well with closely-fitting flat stone slabs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "artefact"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an object that is of historical and cultural value"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Because such a rich array of artefacts and natural remains has been discovered during the various archaeological excavations, archeologists assume that the village was abandoned quickly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to abandon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to leave or desert"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Because such a rich array of artefacts and natural remains has been discovered during the various archaeological excavations, archeologists assume that the village was abandoned quickly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le08ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past  Active and Passive Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past </span>tense to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This tense can have <span class=\"underline\">active</span> and <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> forms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. <span class=\"underline\">Passives</span> without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the examples of the form of both the <span class=\"underline\">active</span> and <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> voices of the <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past</span>:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Active\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">People <span class=\\\"strong\\\">discovered</span> the village of Skara Brae in the winter of 1850.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Passive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The Neolithic village of Skara Brae <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was discovered </span>in the winter of 1850. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Astonishingly, Skara Brae<span class=\"strong\">  was inhabited </span> before the Egyptian pyramids<span class=\"strong\">  were built</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Archeologists assume that the village<span class=\"strong\">  was abandoned</span> quickly. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The site<span class=\"strong\">  was given </span> official recognition in 1999."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It<span class=\"strong\">  was placed</span> on the World Heritage list as a Neolithic site."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about a Neolithic village."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I write a text answering wh- questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare a short presentation on the village site."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Present perfect tense and the Simple Past tense in both Active and Passive voice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give my presentation to a partner small group. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read through the text again."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library to find out about a Neolithic village."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make notes about where the place is, who found it, who lived there and what it looked like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a short presentation on the village site."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your presentation with a partner."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Active and Passive Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect </span>to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This tense can also have <span class=\"underline\">active</span> and <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> forms.<br /><br />Look at the chart for the examples of the form of both the <span class=\"underline\">active</span> and<span class=\"underline\"> passive</span> voices of the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span>:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Active\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> have built</span> the houses well, with closely-fitting flat stone slabs. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Passive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The houses <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been built</span> well with closely-fitting flat stone slabs. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is the degree to which it<span class=\"strong\"> has been preserved</span> that is important."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They<span class=\"strong\"> have been set</span> into large mounds of midden."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They<span class=\"strong\"> have been linked</span> together by covered passageways."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A rich array of artefacts and natural remains <span class=\"strong\">has been discovered</span> during the various archaeological excavations. "}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le08ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le08ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The Neolithic village of Skara Brae was discovered in the winter of 1850. When a wild storm ripped the grass from Skara Brae, it exposed an immense refuse heap. It also brought to light the ruins of ancient stone buildings. These dwellings have proven to be the best-preserved Neolithic village in western Europe.</br></br>Astonishingly, Skara Brae was inhabited before the Egyptian pyramids were built, and flourished for centuries before construction began at Stonehenge. It is 5,000 years old.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le08ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "However, it is not its age that has made it so remarkable. It is the degree to which it has been preserved. The structures of this semi-subterranean village have survived in impressive condition. So, amazingly, has the furniture in the village houses.</br></br>This is a unique window into the past that has allowed us see how people once lived. The site was given official recognition in 1999 when it was placed on the World Heritage list as a Neolithic site.</br></br>What you notice when you go into Skara Brae, is that the houses have been built well with closely-fitting flat stone slabs. They have been set into large mounds of midden and have been linked together by covered passageways. Each house was made up of a single room, about 450 square feet.", "id": 2, "time": "32200", "image": "engenn10le08ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "All of the homes were alike. Stone furniture was fitted into each room. In each a stone dresser, two box-beds and a hearth or fireplace.  A large structure at one end of the village has been identified as a workshop.\n</br></br>Because such a rich array of artefacts and natural remains has been discovered during the various archaeological excavations, archeologists assume that the village was abandoned quickly. Surprisingly, no weapons have been found suggesting they had a peaceful life.", "id": 3, "time": "81000", "image": "engenn10le08ob03re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about history and civilization."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report facts about events or actions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about unusual events in the past. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you know about life in Neolithic times about 5000 years ago?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What type of homes do you think people built at that time?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " It's a Neolithic village!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nThe houses are set into mounds of <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">midden</span>.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts